// ================= Shum Yip Upperhills (SOM towers; URBANUS LOFT; ARQ retail podium) =================
// Tower 1: 388.1 m, 80 storeys (offices below, hotel above, top floor 379.1 m with a restaurant, roof garden and helipad),
// completed 2020; a "ladder core": eight mega-columns, the corners cantilevered 8.5 m and notched (L-shaped corner glazing),
// a 3 m curtain-wall module, belt trusses with louvres at the mechanical floors (CTBUH paper 2915, SOM, Wikipedia).
// Tower 2: 299.3 m, 62 storeys of offices, 2017, the same facade grid (CTBUH, SOM). The ballroom pavilion: a faceted form whose
// folded north, south and roof enclosures span the ballrooms over a 12.5 m high public terrace (SOM). The LOFT (URBANUS): a
// "town" of small buildings, lanes and roof gardens on the 64 000 m2 roof of the retail podium (designboom).
// Footprints: w684494961 (T1), w684494959 (T2), w1393874916 (pavilion), the LOFT blocks w14315013xx and the podium blocks
